[{:adr/authoritative_for ["cloud-itonami-isic-5911 film/TV-production operations-coordination actor implementation" "fresh scaffold closing the kotoba-lang/industry :spec entry gap for ISIC 5911"], :adr/topic "cloud-itonami-isic-5911-motion-picture-production-coverage", :adr/related ["cloud-itonami-isic-873" "ADR-2607121000" "ADR-2607152500"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2620100000-cloud-itonami-isic-5911-motion-picture-production-coverage", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-16", :adr/body "# ADR-2620100000: cloud-itonami-isic-5911 (Motion picture, video and television programme production activities) film/TV-production-operations-coordination actor -- fresh scaffold, full implementation\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-16\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)\n**Related**: ADR-2607121000 (Wave 3, production/robotics), ADR-2607152500\n(Wave 4, human-facing/personal services -- authorizes this batch to\nproceed in parallel with Wave 3), cloud-itonami-isic-873 (Residential\ncare for elderly/disabled -- the Wave 4 flagship reference module shape\nthis actor mirrors, independently re-read in full before use), the\n`kotoba-lang/industry` registry's `\"5911\"` catalog entry\n\n## Context\n\n`kotoba-lang/industry`'s registry carried a `\"5911\"` entry at\n`:maturity :spec` with `:name \"Motion picture, video and television\nprogramme production a...\"` (truncated -- one of the ~10%-of-entries\ntruncated-name seed-data artifacts this fleet has documented elsewhere;\nmatched the assigned ISIC class exactly at the truncation point,\nconfirming no ID/name mismatch, and de-truncated to the full ISIC Rev.4\nname \"Motion picture, video and television programme production\nactivities\" as part of this same promotion) and `:repo\n\"https://github.com/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J5911\"` (an old,\nnever-populated naming scheme). Confirmed no repo exists yet at either\nthat stale placeholder or the real\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5911` target (`gh api` 404 for the\nlatter) before any work began. Sibling classes 5912 (post-production),\n5913 (distribution), and 5914 (projection) are distinct, separately\nbuilt entries in this same batch; 5912's `:name` was confirmed to start\n\"...post-product...\", 5913's \"...distribution...\", 5914's the full,\nuntruncated \"Motion picture projection activities\" -- none conflated\nwith this class's pre-production/production scope.\n\nThis is part of Wave 4 (human-facing/personal-services fleet, ISIC\nsections I/P/Q/R/S/T), running in parallel with the ongoing Wave 3\n(production/robotics) rollout per ADR-2607152500. Film/TV production\ntouches on-set physical-safety and talent-welfare dimensions (stunt\nwork, minor performers, working conditions), so per Wave 4's\nperson-facing-service safety guardrail this actor's closed op allowlist\nmust never include an op that directly finalizes an on-set-safety-\nauthority decision (clearing a stunt as safe, overriding a\nminor-performer work-hour limit) -- those are always either a hard\npermanent block or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible.\n\n## Decision\n\nScaffold `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5911` as a film/TV-production\nOPERATIONS COORDINATION actor (not an on-set-safety authority, not an\nequipment-actuation controller), mirroring `cloud-itonami-isic-873`'s\nverified module shape (`store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`phase`/`operation`/\n`sim`, `deps.edn`/`blueprint.edn`/README/GOVERNANCE/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/\nCONTRIBUTING/SECURITY, AGPL-3.0-or-later) with fresh, film/TV-production-\nspecific domain logic under the `filmprodops` namespace:\n\n1. **`filmprodops.store`** -- `MemStore` (atom of EDN) behind a `Store`\n   protocol; a `productions` directory keyed by `:production-id` STRING\n   (a film/TV production under way), plus an append-only `ledger` and a\n   `coordination-log` of committed records.\n2. **`filmprodops.advisor`** (\"FilmProductionAdvisor\") -- deterministic\n   mock advisor drafting exactly four kinds of proposal: shoot-day/\n   scene/take record logging (`:log-production-record`), shoot-day/\n   location/crew scheduling (`:schedule-production-operation`), on-set\n   safety-concern flagging (`:flag-onset-safety-concern`), and footage/\n   dailies post-production handoff coordination\n   (`:coordinate-post-production-handoff`). Every proposal's `:effect`\n   is always `:propose`; every output is censored downstream by the\n   governor.\n3. **`filmprodops.governor`** (\"FilmProductionGovernor\") -- three HARD\n   checks, all permanent and un-overridable: (1) production-unverified\n   -- the target production record must exist AND be independently\n   `:registered?`/`:verified?` in the store before ANY proposal for it\n   may commit or escalate; (2) effect-not-propose -- any `:effect`\n   other than `:propose` is HARD-blocked; (3) scope-exclusion -- any\n   proposal (regardless of op) whose op/summary/rationale/cites/value\n   touches finalizing an on-set safety-clearance decision (stunt-\n   clearance sign-off, hazard-clearance sign-off), overriding a\n   minor-performer work-hour limit, directly actuating rigging/stunt/\n   pyrotechnic equipment, or finalizing talent-compensation/insurance/\n   legal/union matters is a HARD, PERMANENT block, unconditionally\n   evaluated on every proposal; an op outside the closed four-op\n   allowlist is folded into this same check. One ESCALATE (soft) gate:\n   `:flag-onset-safety-concern` ALWAYS escalates to a human regardless\n   of confidence, as does low confidence generally.\n4. **`filmprodops.phase`** -- Phase 0->3 staged rollout;\n   `:flag-onset-safety-concern` is permanently ABSENT from every\n   phase's `:auto` set (structural fact, not a rollout milestone still\n   to come) -- only `:log-production-record`/`:schedule-production-\n   operation`/`:coordinate-post-production-handoff` may auto-commit at\n   phase 3 when governor-clean.\n5. **`filmprodops.operation`** (\"OperationActor\") -- langgraph-clj\n   StateGraph, `intake -> advise -> govern -> decide -> commit | hold |\n   request-approval`, `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}` for\n   human-in-the-loop sign-off, invoked exclusively via\n   `langgraph.graph/run*`.\n6. **`deps.edn` / `blueprint.edn` / docs** -- mirror\n   `cloud-itonami-isic-873`'s shape (`:test`/`:lint`/`:run`/`:dev`\n   aliases pinned to the same `kotoba-lang/langgraph` git SHA\n   `a332a770a0d2b5193f81b54483bb954fb29ef8d7`, `itonami.blueprint/*`\n   metadata, scope/design/testing README sections).\n\n### Scope-exclusion phrasing discipline (fleet-wide self-tripping bug avoided proactively)\n\nMultiple sibling agents in this batch independently discovered and\nfixed the same bug class: a scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare\nnoun (e.g. \"stunt\", \"minor\") accidentally matches inside the mock\nadvisor's own DEFAULT rationale/disclaimer text for a legitimate,\nallowed proposal, causing the actor to self-block on its own happy\npath. This build avoided that class from the start rather than\ndiscovering it via a failing test: `filmprodops.governor/scope-excluded-\nterms` are phrased exclusively as the finalization/execution ACTION\n(\"finalize the stunt clearance\", \"override the minor performer\nwork-hour limit\"), never as the bare noun alone. A dedicated regression\ntest, `default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip` in\n`test/filmprodops/governor_test.clj`, independently confirms every\nallowed op's own default (clean) advisor-generated proposal text --\nagainst every demo production -- clears the governor's scope-exclusion\nscan.\n\n### What this actor does NOT do\n\nFinalizing an on-set safety-clearance decision (stunt-clearance\nsign-off, hazard-clearance sign-off), overriding or finalizing a\nminor-performer work-hour limit, directly actuating rigging/stunt/\npyrotechnic equipment, and finalizing talent-compensation/contract\nterms or insurance/legal/union matters all remain exclusively\nhuman/institutional decisions, permanently, with no actor or\nhuman-approval override path -- enforced structurally by the\ngovernor's closed op/effect allowlists and the unconditional\nscope-exclusion check, not just documented. `:flag-onset-safety-concern`\nis a \"surface the concern\" op only; it can never self-clear the concern\nit raises, and is never a member of any phase's `:auto` set.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-5911`: `clojure -M:dev:test` -- raw final line:\n  `Ran 41 tests containing 129 assertions.` / `0 failures, 0 errors.`\n  (re-run green a second time from a brand-new fresh clone after push).\n- `clojure -M:lint` -- 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `clojure -M:dev -e \"(require 'filmprodops.sim) (filmprodops.sim/-main)\"`\n  demo narrative exercises proposal submission, escalation/approval on\n  every write op, and every HARD-hold scenario directly (unregistered\n  production, unverified production, non-`:propose` effect, on-set\n  safety-clearance-finalization/minor-performer-hour-override scope\n  drift) -- ran clean, no exceptions; committed coordination log and\n  audit ledger both inspected and match expectations.\n- All source under `src/`/`test/` is `.cljc`, no JVM-only interop; the\n  actor graph is invoked exclusively via `langgraph.graph/run*`.\n- Repo created fresh (`gh repo create` + push, public visibility\n  matching the reference and `blueprint.edn`'s `:status :public-oss`),\n  initial commit `5effb35` on `cloud-itonami-isic-5911`'s `main` (no\n  prior history), confirmed via a brand-new fresh clone (`git log\n  --oneline -1` matches `gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5911/commits/main`).\n- `kotoba-lang/industry` registry `\"5911\"` entry updated in place\n  (exact-text edit of the literal `{:id \"5911\" ...}` block only, no\n  other entry's block touched, byte-offset-diff-verified confined to\n  the intended region): `:name` de-truncated to the full \"Motion\n  picture, video and television programme production activities\",\n  `:repo`/`:business-id` corrected from the never-populated\n  `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J5911` naming to `cloud-itonami/cloud-\n  itonami-isic-5911` / `cloud-itonami-isic-5911`, `:required-\n  technologies` normalized from a stale `[:robotics :identity :forms\n  :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :phone]` placeholder to the coordination-\n  only shape actually implemented `[:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn\n  :audit-ledger]` (matching sibling `cloud-itonami-isic-873`'s own\n  `:required-technologies`), `:maturity` `:spec` -> `:implemented`;\n  `:operating-states` deliberately left unchanged (matching this\n  fleet's established convention of not touching that field on\n  promotion, per sibling `cloud-itonami-isic-5811`/`5629` precedent).\n  Landed via a Contents API single-file PUT (sha-checked optimistic\n  concurrency; succeeded on the first attempt, no sha drift observed),\n  commit `849142cb21b19c3bf4b4a2b9d7fdb5579c66fdce`.\n- `test/kotoba/industry_test.clj`'s `maturity-summary` assertion\n  bumped, live-recomputed via `(kotoba.industry/maturity-summary)`\n  against freshly re-fetched registry.edn content immediately before\n  the PUT attempt (never a reused/stale buffer) -- this file is an\n  extremely hot, high-concurrency shared file across the fleet; the\n  first attempt hit no sha conflict and landed directly, bumping the\n  assertion from a stale `383` to the true live `385` (reflecting\n  concurrent sibling promotions landed in the same window, not just\n  this one), commit `9a4b7910d0279c2eb44955570cc7cee6e1d35100`.\n- Full `kotoba-lang/industry` suite re-run green after all edits (fresh\n  clone, plus a fresh `kotoba-lang/technology` sibling clone for\n  `deps.edn` resolution): `Ran 15 tests containing 1048 assertions.` /\n  `0 failures, 0 errors.`\n- Final post-merge re-verification (brand-new scratch directory, fresh\n  `origin/main` clone of both `cloud-itonami-isic-5911` and\n  `kotoba-lang/industry`, plus a fresh `kotoba-lang/technology`\n  sibling): `clojure -M:dev:test` / `clojure -M:test` re-run green in\n  both repos; the registry's `\"5911\"` entry confirmed `:maturity\n  :implemented` with the corrected `:name`/`:repo`/`:business-id`/\n  `:required-technologies`, and a sample of sibling entries\n  (`873`/`6310`/`5811`/`5912`/`5913`/`5914`) confirmed untouched (5912/\n  5913/5914 independently found already `:implemented` by concurrent\n  sibling agents in this same batch, consistent with this ADR's own\n  Context section). `grep`/Python scan for the UTF-8 replacement\n  character against `resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` returned\n  `0` (no file-wide mojibake).\n\n## Consequences\n\n(+) `cloud-itonami-isic-5911` now has a real, tested implementation\nmatching the shape of every other cloud-itonami ISIC actor, replacing a\n`:spec` placeholder pointing at a repo that never existed.\n\n(+) `kotoba-lang/industry` registry `\"5911\"` entry promoted to\n`:maturity :implemented`.\n\n(+) This actor is another concrete example of Wave 4's person-facing-\nservice safety guardrail applied to a distinct sensitive-decision axis:\non-set physical-safety/talent-welfare authority (stunt clearance,\nminor-performer work-hour limits) rather than clinical-care or\neditorial-content authority, all folded into one unconditional\nscope-exclusion check that never trusts the advisor's own framing of\nits intent, and phrased from the start as finalization-ACTION terms\n(not bare nouns) to avoid the fleet-known self-tripping bug class.\n\n(-) Still a simulation/proposal layer, not a real production-management\nsystem. On-set safety-clearance decisions, minor-performer work-hour\ncompliance, and equipment actuation remain human-/institution-\ncontrolled via external channels.\n\n(-) No integration with real production-management systems (call sheet/\nscheduling software, insurance/COI tracking, SAG-AFTRA/union\ncompliance systems, dailies/DIT pipelines) -- this is a standalone\ncoordinator blueprint, matching every prior sibling actor's own stated\nlimitation.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n| Option | Verdict | Reason |\n|---|---|---|\n| Bundle on-set safety clearance as an always-escalate op the actor can still draft | ❌ | Wave 4's guardrail requires that no op directly finalize an on-set-safety-authority decision; even an escalate-only \"draft a stunt clearance\" op would imply the actor participates in constructing that decision, so it is excluded entirely via the closed op allowlist plus the HARD scope-exclusion check, not merely gated |\n| Phrase scope-exclusion terms as bare nouns (\"stunt\", \"minor\") for simplicity | ❌ | Directly the fleet-known self-tripping bug class -- a legitimate `:flag-onset-safety-concern` proposal must be free to say \"stunt\" when reporting a real stunt-risk observation; phrasing exclusions as the finalization ACTION avoids the collision structurally |\n| Keep `cloud-itonami-isic-5911` at `:spec` only | ❌ | Wave 4 is actively building out the human-facing-services fleet in parallel with Wave 3; this class was unclaimed and ready for a fresh scaffold, mirroring the now-standard `cloud-itonami-isic-873` shape |\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607121000 (Wave 3, production/robotics)\n- ADR-2607152500 (Wave 4, human-facing/personal services)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-873` (Residential care activities for the elderly\n  and disabled -- the Wave 4 flagship reference module shape)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-5912`/`5913`/`5914` (sibling Motion Picture\n  division classes built in this same batch)\n- `kotoba-lang/industry` `resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn`\n  (fleet-wide maturity registry)\n", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-16", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2620100000: cloud-itonami-isic-5911 (Motion picture, video and television programme production activities) film/TV-production-operations-coordination actor -- fresh scaffold, full implementation", :adr/source-format "edn"}]